AIM To study the basic hardware components of computer networking and
understand the functions of common networking devices.

THEORY 1. A computer network connects computers and devices to share
data, resources, and services. 2. Network Interface Card (NIC): Connects
a computer to a wired or wireless network. It has a unique MAC address.
3. Hub: Connects devices in a LAN and broadcasts incoming data to all
its ports. 4. Switch: Connects devices in a LAN and forwards frames
using MAC addresses. It reduces unnecessary traffic. 5. Router: Connects
different networks and forwards packets using IP addresses. 6. Modem:
Converts signals as required for communication through an internet
service provider. 7. Repeater: Regenerates weak signals to extend the
communication distance. 8. Bridge: Connects LAN segments and filters
traffic between them. 9. Wireless Access Point: Allows wireless devices
to connect to a wired network through Wi-Fi. 10. Transmission media:
Twisted-pair and fibre-optic cables carry data through wired
connections; radio waves carry data wirelessly. 11. Hub works by
broadcasting data, whereas a switch sends frames to the required port
when the destination is known. 12. A router selects the next path for a
packet using its routing table.

PROCEDURE / WORKING 1. Identify the available networking devices and
observe their ports and indicators. 2. Identify Ethernet cables, RJ-45
connectors, and wireless antennas. 3. Study the purpose of each device
and compare hub, switch, and router. 4. Trace a typical connection:
computer → switch → router → internet. 5. Record the name and function
of each component.

CONCLUSION The basic networking hardware components and their functions
were studied. Their roles in connecting devices and transferring data
were understood.

